ttps://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T02:23:55Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T02:24:47Z","body":"This took me roughly ~100 tries to reproduce once. Interesting, has_mouse did not switch to false on mine like it did in the OP's log. Perhaps the exit events are somehow getting merged?\n\n```\n1716: mouse_pos (6066, 2113),  window_rect [P: (4984, 1816), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n1717: mouse_pos (5818, 2141),  window_rect [P: (4984, 1816), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n1717: mouse_pos (5553, 2158),  window_rect [P: (4984, 1816), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n1718: mouse_pos (5295, 2171),  window_rect [P: (4984, 1816), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n1719: exited\n1719: entered\n1719: mouse_pos (4807, 2183),  window_rect [P: (4984, 1816), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:false)\n```\n\n> Godot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080 Ti (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.3713) - AMD Ryzen 9 3900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3034222954/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035237795","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108240#issuecomment-3035237795","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108240","id":3035237795,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc606g2j","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T09:43:09Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T09:43:09Z","body":"Try as I might, couldn't replicate on Fedora Linux 42 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition).\n\nTried both `v4.4.1.stable` and `v4.5.beta2`. Tried Next Play floating and not floating. Tried without embedding. Tried different window sizes. Tried clicking both inside and outside the window after moving the mouse through and the only thing different was that _sometimes_, when clicking outside the window it would report the mouse position after the mouse exited signal, which doesn't seem relevant here.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0be5d764-3487-41ef-a074-31c313c8ab58)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035237795/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035595595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108240#issuecomment-3035595595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108240","id":3035595595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6074NL","user":{"login":"rxlecky","id":35656626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjU2NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35656626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky","html_url":"https://github.com/rxlecky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T10:58:08Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T10:58:08Z","body":"> Is this still an issue if the control doesn't cover the entire screen?\n\nGood shout! I tested this now and it seems that it only happens consistently when the mouse is exiting both the control and the window at the same time. So the control doesn't need to _cover_ the window but it needs to be close enough to the window edge so that the mouse leaves the control and the window at roughly the same time - presumably within a single frame or input event loop.\n\nI will update the issue title to reflect this important detail.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035595595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035695916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108240#issuecomment-3035695916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108240","id":3035695916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc608Qss","user":{"login":"rxlecky","id":35656626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjU2NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35656626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky","html_url":"https://github.com/rxlecky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T11:18:58Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T11:18:58Z","body":"> This took me roughly ~100 tries to reproduce once. \n\nInteresting! I was able to reproduce very easily and consistently. It makes me wonder if it's related to the fact that you're on Win10. Since it's looking like it may be a platform specific issue I would not rule it out.\n\n>  Interesting, has_mouse did not switch to false on mine like it did in the OP's log. Perhaps the exit events are somehow getting merged?\n\nBy this do you mean that the input event prior to the exited signal reports `has_mouse: true`? Notice that that event was fired one tick earlier. The event that was fired on the same tick as the entered and exited signals already reports `has_mouse: false`. So that looks correct to me - or at least in line with my findings and logs.\n\nJust for added context, the log I posted in the original bug report has **two** input events fired on the same physics tick - one before  and one after the exited and entered signals are emitted - and both report `has_mouse: false`. However, it is not always the case that there are two events fired. Here's log from another reproduction case where only one input event is triggered on the same tick, after the exited and entered signals:\n\n```\n120: entered\n120: mouse_pos (1675, 1215),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n121: mouse_pos (1684, 1089),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n122: mouse_pos (1694, 1015),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n124: mouse_pos (1695, 1011),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n125: mouse_pos (1695, 1010),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n126: mouse_pos (1696, 1010),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n127: mouse_pos (1690, 1045),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n128: mouse_pos (1685, 1067),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n129: mouse_pos (1667, 1177),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:true)\n130: exited\n130: entered\n130: mouse_pos (1633, 1413),  window_rect [P: (1344, 726), S: (1152, 648)](has_mouse:false)\n```\n\nFor completeness, I will say that I only ever reproduced the issue with these two variations of input events ordering. It was either two events, one before and one after the exited and entered signals, or one event after the exited and entered signals, but never one event before the exited and entered signals - or more than two events in a single tick.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035695916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3036613049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108240#issuecomment-3036613049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108240","id":3036613049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60_wm5","user":{"login":"rxlecky","id":35656626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjU2NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35656626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky","html_url":"https://github.com/rxlecky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rxlecky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T15:05:03Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T15:05:03Z","body":"I had a bit of time to git bisect the issue and managed to pinpoint the bug to 945babc619cee143f56219b9182b8392edd4eeb3. I can't debug further right now but I'm throwing it out there if anyone who wants to investigate.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3036613049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256420282","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108240#issuecomment-3256420282","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108240","id":3256420282,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CGQe6","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T23:44:12Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T23:44:12Z","body":"I can confirm that pr #89920 is the cause of this regression. Readd the early return removed in the mentioned pr or replace `p_pos` for `Viewport::get_mouse_position()` in this part seems to fix the issue\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6c9aa4c7d3b9b91cd50714c40eeb234874df7075/scene/main/viewport.cpp#L3249-L3251\n\n<br>\n\nCC @Sauermann ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issue